{"name":"Cruising","hex":"#018498","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cruising","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sailing about without an exact destination, especially for pleasure.","Driving around without an exact destination, as a social activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of cruise"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cruising"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cruise ship","blocks":[{"text":"Cruise ships are large passenger ships used mainly for vacationing. Unlike ocean liners, which are used for transport, cruise ships typically embark on round-trip voyages to various ports of call, where passengers may go on shore excursions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Icon_of_the_Seas_Puerto_Rico_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Icon_of_the_Seas_Puerto_Rico_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruise_ship","wikidata":"Q39804"},{"title":"Cruising (driving)","blocks":[{"text":"Cruising is a social activity that primarily consists of driving a car. Cruising is distinguished from regular driving by the social and recreational nature of the activity, which is characterized by an impulsively random, often aimless course. A popular route is often the focus of cruising. Cruising can be an expression of the freedom of possessing a driver's license. \"Cruise nights\" are evenings during which cars drive slowly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Cruise_on_Colby_%2817662461654%29.jpg/330px-Cruise_on_Colby_%2817662461654%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruising_(driving)","wikidata":"Q444310"},{"title":"Cruising (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cruising is a 1980 crime thriller written and directed by William Friedkin, and starring Al Pacino, Paul Sorvino and Karen Allen. It is loosely based on the 1970 novel by The New York Times reporter Gerald Walker about a serial killer targeting gay men, particularly the men associated with the leather scene. The title is a double entendre, as \"cruising\" can describe both police officers on patrol and men who are cruising for sex. It was an international co-production between West Germany and the United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f9/Cruisingposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cruising_(film)","wikidata":"Q952511"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/M_s_galaxy.jpg/500px-M_s_galaxy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/M_s_galaxy.jpg/1280px-M_s_galaxy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/M_s_galaxy.jpg/500px-M_s_galaxy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cruiseferry MS Galaxy at the port of Mariehamn, Åland, in February 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AM_s_galaxy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG/500px-MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG/1280px-MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG/500px-MSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cruise ships MSC Poesia, Vision of the Seas, and Mein Schiff Herz at Tallinn Passenger Port in Estonia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMSC_Poesia_Vision_of_the_Seas_%26_Mein_Schiff_2_in_Tallinn_13_June_2012.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/C1950_PO_Liner_Strathaird.jpg/500px-C1950_PO_Liner_Strathaird.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/C1950_PO_Liner_Strathaird.jpg/500px-C1950_PO_Liner_Strathaird.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"RMS Strathaird, a P&O ocean liner that sometimes served as a cruise ship. The company began offering luxury cruise services in 1944.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AC1950_PO_Liner_Strathaird.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg/500px-Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg/1280px-Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg/500px-Prinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prinzessin Victoria Luise was the first purpose-built cruise ship.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrinzessin_Victoria_Luise_LOC_det.4a15439.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/QE2_WEB.jpg/500px-QE2_WEB.jpg?ut